{{Wireless embedded system |brand=IP-COM |model=W63AP |series=AC1200 |fcc_date=03/22/2019 |manuf_country=China |is_manuf=No |manuf=Tenda |manuf_model=i24 |type=access point |fcc_id=2ABZMW63AP, V7TI24 |pcb_id=10038683 V1.0 |pwr_v=12 |pwr_amp=1.5 |pwr_conn=barrel |cpu1_brand=Qualcomm Atheros |cpu1_model=QCA9531 |wi1_chip1_brand=Qualcomm Atheros |wi1_chip1_model=QCA9531 |wi1_802dot11_protocols=bgn |wi1_txchains=2 |wi1_rxchains=2 |wi1_sstreams=2 |wi2_chip1_brand=Qualcomm Atheros |wi2_chip1_model=QCA9886 |wi2_802dot11_protocols=an+ac |wi2_txchains=2 |wi2_rxchains=2 |wi2_sstreams=2 |eth_cpu=true |eth_chip2_brand=Qualcomm Atheros |eth_chip2_model=QCA8334;Q, QCA8334-AL3C, PK82193P, 1821, TAIWAN |lan_speed=1G |lan_ports=1 |flags=Wave2, MU-MIMO, |802dot11_protocols=abgn+ac |default_ip=192.168.0.254 |default_user=admin |default_pass=admin }} {{TagLine|AC1200 Wave2 Gigabit Access Point}}
FCC ID 2ABZMW63AP is a change in ID request from V7TI24 of the [[Tenda i24]]. [[Qualcomm]] CPU and radio chip IDs are not shown in the FCC internal photos. The CPU is assumed to be a QCA9531 like what's in the [[Tenda W15E V2]]. WI2 is likely a QCA9886 since it is 2x2 and supports MU-MIMO.
"10038683" and "V1.0" are silkscreened on the board in the FCC photos.
